                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "NOTE: The online multiplayer in this game is 100% broken, and the online portion is the reason I intended to play this game. The lag I experienced was so bad that you can't even move around without a huge delay. There is a warning when you access the online mode telling you that it's experimental, but you'll only realize this after playing the game. They don't mention it on the store page or anywhere else as far as I know.\n\nAVOID the game at all costs if online MP is all you're looking for. Now, onto reviewing the other parts of the game.\n\nPros:\n\n+ Cool original character designs, nice animations and sprites. Good overall graphics.\n+ Some of the levels were more challenging than I was expecting and work well with the scorpion \"get over here\" move.\n+ The AI for the bots is pretty good if you plan on playing the game alone, and in certain game modes provide a good challenge.\n\nCons:\n\n- Scorpion gimmick gets old fast, providing maybe an hour or so of gameplay before the fun runs out.\n- Bots sometimes don't attack you after they've stunned you, which makes overcoming them a little too easy occasionally.\n- No real incentive to keep you playing, there's no campaign or rewards for winning. Would be nice if they added unlockable characters, costumes, or literally any kind of reward for progressing. It doesn't even have achievements.\n- As stated before, the online multiplayer is completely broken. I'm willing to try almost any game, no matter how bad it is in online MP so the lack of it is very disappointing.\n\nFor a local multiplayer game, it's probably not too bad but there are much better multiplayer arena games you can play and the scorpion gimmick isn't really adding anything you can't live without. Not worth the $9.99. If you're intent on buying it, only get this if you can get it for $0.50 or in a bundle.",
